  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Musalaha Youth Center Bethlehem</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project empowers young people so that they will have the tools to make a change in their local communities. This will be accomplished by equipping and empowering Muslim and Christian youth leaders to transform Palestinian society and create inter religious dialogue and thereby creating peaceful coexistence in a context of religious division. This project targets both men and women of different religious, social, and political backgrounds. The project will establish a youth group of 30 young Palestinians in the Bethlehem area and will focus on creating a Youth Center in Bethlehem and three outreach groups that will focus on education/culture, social media, and environment. The group will meet and be empowered through two major events addressing reconciliation, volunteerism, and leadership and 8 monthly meetings.</narrative>
  </description>
